A||||2||PTW87GT||Parking Brake Light||||1||
Z||000000||PTW87GT||01-25-2001||08:21 AM||||My parking brake light stays on as much as my engine.  Does anyone know how to disconnect or adjust?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Carrolles||01-25-2001||09:12 AM||||The switch is at the base of the parking brake handle.  Remove the trim piece that runs from under the dash to the pillar behind the seat.  There are about 6 or so small hex head (maybe torx head) screws with snap in metal caps covering them.  Carefully pry the trim piece up and out to get to the brake lever.<P>Remove the boot covering the handle mechanism and you will see a switch at the base of the mechanism.  Your brake handle may not be returning far enough to turn off the light.<P>Are you sure it is the parking brake that is causing the light?  I believe the "Brake" light is used by both the parking brake and the brake master cylinder.  <P>The hydraulic system of the brakes is actually two sets of seals on one piston rod.  This separates the brake hydraulics into two circuits.  If a leak developes in a caliper you won't necessarily lose the entire brakes because of this.  There is a switch in the master cylinder that monitors the pressure in both sides of the hydraulic circuit and illuminates if it senses higher pressure in one side. <P>I'd take a hard look at the brakes to see if they are ok and not assume that it is just the parking brake switch.<P>Hope this helps,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000002||PTW87GT||01-25-2001||03:24 PM||||Yes, When I move the brake handle it goes out until the button comes back out.  Thanks for your help.||||reg||1
